WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.140
Section one.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.442
The problem and the product.

00:00:05.584 --> 00:00:07.644
GitHub Manager helps you discover,

00:00:08.784 --> 00:00:10.624
understand, and organize repositories.

00:00:11.865 --> 00:00:14.825
The purpose is to turn a scattered collection into

00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:18.806
a workspace whose relationships you can inspect and change.

00:00:28.807 --> 00:00:30.367
Imagine starting an API project.

00:00:31.759 --> 00:00:32.959
You have your own services,

00:00:33.719 --> 00:00:36.619
shared repositories, and libraries starred for later.

00:00:38.511 --> 00:00:40.511
Names and programming languages help you search.

00:00:41.424 --> 00:00:44.464
They do not explain which pieces support the same

00:00:44.464 --> 00:00:44.924
initiative.

00:00:46.756 --> 00:00:50.456
Two Python repositories may serve entirely different purposes.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.620
GitHub remains the source of repository facts:

00:00:59.660 --> 00:00:59.780
identity,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:00.580
links,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.100
visibility, and available metadata.

00:01:04.369 --> 00:01:07.009
The application builds selected evidence locally.

00:01:08.157 --> 00:01:11.637
AI proposes an organization, and the user reviews it.

00:01:12.466 --> 00:01:16.825
This separation matters because a convenient suggestion must not

00:01:16.825 --> 00:01:19.726
quietly replace a fact or a deliberate decision.

00:01:24.887 --> 00:01:28.867
We will follow Orion, an authored synthetic patient-intake

00:01:28.867 --> 00:01:29.467
application.

00:01:31.097 --> 00:01:35.457
Its displayed classification comes from a saved real API

00:01:35.457 --> 00:01:35.977
test.

00:01:37.287 --> 00:01:40.807
We will also use a public FastAPI library as

00:01:40.807 --> 00:01:41.467
a contrast.

00:01:42.877 --> 00:01:46.537
These examples explain the mechanics; they are not a

00:01:46.537 --> 00:01:48.877
new account recording or a new benchmark.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.420
Section two.

00:01:56.633 --> 00:01:57.773
Organization vocabulary.

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:02.487
Before classification, we need to define what a relationship

00:02:02.487 --> 00:02:03.007
means.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.060
The purpose is to keep an initiative, a capability,

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.360
and a technology from becoming one confusing pile of

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:11.480
labels.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.540
A Project answers which product or initiative a repository

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.040
supports.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:29.288
A Domain groups those Projects into a broader area.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.996
A Topic describes a primary capability or subject.

00:02:35.124 --> 00:02:38.844
A Tag describes technology or another useful characteristic.

00:02:40.312 --> 00:02:43.112
For Orion, the examples are the clinical platform,

00:02:43.832 --> 00:02:46.092
Healthcare, Web APIs, and Python.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.110
A repository may support more than one Project.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.440
Its Domains derive through those Project memberships;

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.740
the classifier does not assign Domains independently.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.850
Topics and Tags remain useful when no Project applies.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.560
The application's Topics are separate from the native topics

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:12.500
supplied by GitHub.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:21.530
The Orion application uses FastAPI and Python.

00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:26.509
The FastAPI library is itself a reusable framework.

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:30.827
Sharing those words does not make the library part

00:03:30.827 --> 00:03:31.367
of Orion.

00:03:32.646 --> 00:03:36.246
Under the primary-label policy, incidental capabilities are

00:03:36.246 --> 00:03:39.906
omitted, and a library's own name is not automatically

00:03:39.906 --> 00:03:41.146
its dependency Tag.

00:03:42.645 --> 00:03:46.425
Next, we decide what evidence can support that distinction.

00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:52.797
Section three.

00:03:54.495 --> 00:03:55.175
Context engineering.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:59.394
Its purpose is to choose what information the model

00:03:59.394 --> 00:03:59.834
sees,

00:04:00.574 --> 00:04:04.014
what that information means, and which boundaries remain outside

00:04:04.014 --> 00:04:04.494
the model.

00:04:06.232 --> 00:04:09.512
A longer prompt is not automatically a better decision.

00:04:18.533 --> 00:04:21.393
We separate trusted source facts,

00:04:22.793 --> 00:04:26.233
untrusted repository prose, user-owned organization,

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.453
and execution identity.

00:04:29.793 --> 00:04:30.653
Canonical IDs,

00:04:31.633 --> 00:04:31.953
rejections,

00:04:32.753 --> 00:04:35.693
revisions, and evidence hashes constrain the operation.

00:04:36.833 --> 00:04:39.733
The application does not send every stored record to

00:04:39.733 --> 00:04:40.173
the model.

00:04:41.153 --> 00:04:41.873
For example,

00:04:42.533 --> 00:04:46.313
protected decisions filter candidates before prompting rather than

00:04:46.313 --> 00:04:48.793
becoming an entire conversation history.

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:58.010
Hosted input is restricted to verified public repositories and

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:00.070
synthetic fixtures in this implementation.

00:05:02.555 --> 00:05:06.195
Private or unknown visibility fails closed, including phrases

00:05:06.195 --> 00:05:07.615
derived from private text.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.840
Local rules can still help organization.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.126
Narrow cleaning patterns are hygiene,

00:05:15.786 --> 00:05:19.026
not a complete secret scanner or prompt-injection defense.

00:05:20.871 --> 00:05:22.891
The model has no tools with which to act

00:05:22.891 --> 00:05:24.071
on README instructions.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.800
The working runtime is local Next.js,

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.680
FastAPI, and SQLite.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:39.200
LangChain connects structured requests; it does not own the

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.160
application's memory.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:44.680
During development, user decisions outrank approved design,

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.740
plans, and historical discussion.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.280
Phase zero checked access;

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.160
phase zero point five checked AI readiness;

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.600
phase zero point nine delivered the local app.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.620
Cloud runtime remains deferred.

00:06:03.787 --> 00:06:04.667
Section four.

00:06:06.277 --> 00:06:07.237
Evidence and chunking.

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:11.127
The purpose is to preserve the sentence that explains

00:06:11.127 --> 00:06:14.767
a repository, while excluding material that is unlikely to

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:15.567
help organization.

00:06:16.897 --> 00:06:20.717
We begin with a README, not an AI-generated summary.

00:06:29.837 --> 00:06:34.617
The extractor parses Markdown blocks and applies heading-based

00:06:34.617 --> 00:06:35.137
selection.

00:06:36.257 --> 00:06:38.257
Metadata becomes evidence zero;

00:06:39.457 --> 00:06:42.057
selected README text receives additional IDs.

00:06:43.257 --> 00:06:47.777
For Orion, evidence one says: patient intake API

00:06:47.777 --> 00:06:50.137
for the Orion Clinical Platform.

00:06:50.917 --> 00:06:53.457
Uses FastAPI and Python.

00:06:54.257 --> 00:06:56.277
The language metadata is empty,

00:06:56.917 --> 00:07:00.157
so Python is supported by prose rather than an

00:07:00.157 --> 00:07:01.577
invented GitHub value.

00:07:06.847 --> 00:07:09.447
The input byte ceiling limits the fetched document.

00:07:10.902 --> 00:07:13.942
Selected blocks and total evidence have character bounds.

00:07:15.217 --> 00:07:19.817
The compact classification profile then keeps metadata, up to

00:07:19.817 --> 00:07:22.757
two README records, and up to eight phrase strings.

00:07:24.312 --> 00:07:26.412
Exact request tokens are counted later.

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:31.047
Hashes bind the selected content and configuration.

00:07:32.642 --> 00:07:36.482
Offsets identify cleaned text, not original README line numbers.

00:07:42.063 --> 00:07:45.603
Heading rules are inspectable and avoid a hosted summarization

00:07:45.603 --> 00:07:49.543
pass, but can cut sentences or crowd out better

00:07:49.543 --> 00:07:49.963
evidence.

00:07:51.789 --> 00:07:56.149
Format noise, late negation, and multilingual headings need tests.

00:07:57.294 --> 00:08:00.334
The app received a separately versioned cleanup wrapper;

00:08:01.354 --> 00:08:03.854
frozen benchmark profiles stayed unchanged.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:09.540
Retrieval can see full selected evidence that compact generation

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:09.920
omits,

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.740
so both stages need their own checks.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:18.950
Section five.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:20.620
Local algorithms.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:25.190
Their purpose is to expose compact signals before an

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.030
expensive decision.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:31.000
We use phrase extraction and corpus counts, but those

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.620
numbers do not establish initiative membership or semantic

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:35.260
understanding.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:47.860
RAKE splits around stopwords and punctuation.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:52.280
Word frequency and co-occurrence contribute to phrase scores.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:55.680
Our configuration considers one to four words,

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:57.720
retains up to twenty candidates,

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.340
normalizes duplicates, and checks source spans.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:02.700
In Orion,

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.200
patient intake API and Orion clinical platform each score

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:07.660
nine.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.980
FastAPI and Python score one.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.720
Those are weights, not probabilities.

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:23.040
YAKE was compared offline using local document features such

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:23.800
as position,

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:26.060
capitalization, and frequency.

00:09:27.155 --> 00:09:29.515
It is not the production extractor.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:34.910
Its measured runtime included repeated process startup, so the

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:37.190
ratio is not an intrinsic speed comparison.

00:09:39.365 --> 00:09:42.365
Corpus document frequency counts a term once per repository.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:47.900
That pretest table is different from the concept-document IDF

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.160
used in retrieval.

00:09:50.895 --> 00:09:54.435
The installed YAKE artifact's licensing also remained an adoption

00:09:54.435 --> 00:09:54.915
concern.

00:10:00.297 --> 00:10:02.577
A bag of phrases loses relationships,

00:10:03.317 --> 00:10:04.457
including the word not.

00:10:05.843 --> 00:10:07.263
Purpose prose must survive.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:11.030
In one historical FastAPI ablation,

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:15.530
adding RAKE phrases used more input tokens without changing

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:17.310
the unwanted secondary labels.

00:10:18.176 --> 00:10:21.756
That single case proves neither that phrases always help

00:10:22.296 --> 00:10:23.676
nor that they are unnecessary.

00:10:25.963 --> 00:10:29.423
The product also has no learned project-clustering engine or

00:10:29.423 --> 00:10:31.023
automatically learned rules.

00:10:36.513 --> 00:10:37.547
Section six.

00:10:37.547 --> 00:10:39.147
Taxonomy intelligence.

00:10:40.321 --> 00:10:43.161
The purpose is to propose a vocabulary for a

00:10:43.161 --> 00:10:43.281
collection.

00:10:44.515 --> 00:10:47.395
This is different from assigning labels to one repository.

00:10:48.989 --> 00:10:50.889
Discovery can suggest new concepts;

00:10:51.789 --> 00:10:54.469
classification must use concepts already approved.

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:07.670
The saved discovery request contained thirty compact profiles:

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:09.630
ten public samples

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.830
and twenty authored fixtures.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:13.990
Orion's API,

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:15.070
UI,

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:19.310
booking, and audit records supplied related purpose evidence.

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:24.210
The model proposed Orion Clinical Platform with a Clinical

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:27.730
Operations parent and supporting repository IDs.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:31.910
Its twenty proposals were a draft, not a published

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:32.610
organization.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:41.700
The app samples owner and language buckets using a

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.580
deterministic round-robin approach.

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:49.550
Collection packing uses a conservative byte allowance before exact

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:50.290
token counting,

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.690
shortening records and pruning phrases where necessary.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:57.700
This can miss structure outside the cohort.

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:03.190
The saved direct collection request used its original packing

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:06.510
path, so its token counts cannot be attributed to

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:07.670
a later optimization.

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:15.820
Publication normalizes names and aliases,

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:19.520
including Unicode handling, and checks reservations.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:23.160
A visible name can conflict with an alias or

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.260
archived concept.

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:29.020
The app exposes the conflicting record and offers opt-in

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:29.560
reuse,

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:30.520
renaming,

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:32.180
removal, or exclusion.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:36.360
These deterministic checks protect canonical consistency.

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:41.020
Similar language is not permission for an automatic semantic

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:41.440
merge.

00:12:47.523 --> 00:12:48.083
Section seven.

00:12:48.763 --> 00:12:49.683
Retrieval.

00:12:50.183 --> 00:12:53.343
Its purpose is to find plausible concepts from the

00:12:53.343 --> 00:12:54.423
approved vocabulary.

00:12:55.703 --> 00:12:59.603
The repository evidence is the query; concept names,

00:13:00.483 --> 00:13:03.183
definitions, and aliases are the searchable documents.

00:13:04.063 --> 00:13:06.063
A shortlist is not a decision.

00:13:15.757 --> 00:13:19.517
The method called TF-IDF in the code is actually

00:13:19.517 --> 00:13:20.957
binary-IDF cosine.

00:13:22.311 --> 00:13:26.431
It weights less common registry terms and normalizes overlap,

00:13:27.211 --> 00:13:29.571
while repeated terms do not increase frequency.

00:13:30.925 --> 00:13:34.465
A name or alias whose tokens all appear adds

00:13:34.465 --> 00:13:36.425
three once.

00:13:36.939 --> 00:13:39.459
Token order and positive assertion are not required.

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:44.733
Positive candidates are ranked by kind, with stable-ID ties

00:13:44.733 --> 00:13:46.153
and bounded limits.

00:13:51.983 --> 00:13:54.943
Orion retrieves its own Project, Web APIs,

00:13:55.723 --> 00:13:57.303
FastAPI, and Python.

00:13:58.743 --> 00:14:01.883
Forge also surfaces through platform, and Package Management

00:14:01.883 --> 00:14:02.703
through Python.

00:14:03.503 --> 00:14:06.543
The strong Orion score includes the alias boost.

00:14:07.583 --> 00:14:08.903
These are ranking scores,

00:14:09.723 --> 00:14:11.103
not membership probabilities.

00:14:12.463 --> 00:14:15.823
The next stage must distinguish actual purpose evidence from

00:14:15.823 --> 00:14:17.223
distracting shared words.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:26.480
BM25 was compared offline with the same alias boost

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:27.560
and candidate caps.

00:14:29.148 --> 00:14:32.608
It adds saturated term frequency and document-length

00:14:32.608 --> 00:14:33.348
normalization.

00:14:35.216 --> 00:14:36.576
On the small reused comparison,

00:14:37.256 --> 00:14:40.196
both lexical methods covered the expected evaluation labels;

00:14:41.036 --> 00:14:42.476
alias-only missed four Topics.

00:14:43.625 --> 00:14:45.205
That supports feasibility,

00:14:45.924 --> 00:14:48.065
not sparse superiority over dense search.

00:14:49.933 --> 00:14:53.673
There is no embedding query, neural reranker, or autonomous

00:14:53.673 --> 00:14:55.573
retrieval agent in the current product.

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:01.220
Section eight.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:02.140
Augmentation.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:06.520
The purpose is to assemble a decision-ready request from

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:09.140
the evidence and retrieved possibilities.

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:11.740
Retrieval supplies options.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:16.100
Augmentation explains those options and the rules for selecting

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:16.540
them.

00:15:25.427 --> 00:15:29.107
For Orion, the payload includes repository identity,

00:15:30.007 --> 00:15:31.467
public or synthetic source status,

00:15:32.187 --> 00:15:32.407
revision,

00:15:33.307 --> 00:15:33.687
evidence hash,

00:15:34.507 --> 00:15:37.567
selected evidence, phrase strings, and candidate records.

00:15:38.967 --> 00:15:41.787
Evidence one preserves the patient-intake sentence.

00:15:42.687 --> 00:15:46.807
Candidate records contain canonical ID, kind, name, and

00:15:46.807 --> 00:15:47.187
description.

00:15:48.267 --> 00:15:51.547
Aliases helped retrieval but are not serialized into those

00:15:51.547 --> 00:15:52.387
candidate objects.

00:15:53.467 --> 00:15:55.927
Expected evaluation labels are never supplied.

00:16:00.793 --> 00:16:03.893
The system instructions require supported approved IDs,

00:16:04.873 --> 00:16:05.773
primary-purpose Topics,

00:16:06.393 --> 00:16:08.113
and primary implementation Tags.

00:16:09.101 --> 00:16:12.201
Shared frameworks do not prove initiative membership.

00:16:13.748 --> 00:16:14.568
Negation matters;

00:16:15.708 --> 00:16:16.788
multiple Projects are allowed.

00:16:17.955 --> 00:16:20.975
Unsupported input can produce no match or a request

00:16:20.975 --> 00:16:22.055
for more context.

00:16:23.643 --> 00:16:27.323
User decisions remain application constraints rather than an

00:16:27.323 --> 00:16:29.343
invitation for the model to overrule them.

00:16:34.227 --> 00:16:37.047
A strict response schema describes assignments,

00:16:37.867 --> 00:16:38.387
evidence references,

00:16:39.147 --> 00:16:39.447
reasons,

00:16:40.067 --> 00:16:41.226
status, and summary.

00:16:41.226 --> 00:16:44.746
LangChain binds that schema to the hosted request.

00:16:46.165 --> 00:16:49.565
The harness inspects the assembled messages and schema before

00:16:49.565 --> 00:16:50.745
counting input tokens.

00:16:51.964 --> 00:16:55.784
This is retrieval-augmented structured classification, with

00:16:55.784 --> 00:16:57.244
durable application memory.

00:16:58.103 --> 00:17:02.623
It is not a conversational document-question-answering agent, and

00:17:02.623 --> 00:17:05.503
adaptive budgets do not turn it into Adaptive RAG.

00:17:10.733 --> 00:17:11.753
Section nine.

00:17:13.197 --> 00:17:14.797
Generation and validation.

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:19.300
The purpose is to turn the assembled context into

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:20.340
a bounded proposal,

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:23.260
then check it before it affects organization.

00:17:25.343 --> 00:17:27.783
Valid JSON is only the beginning of that check.

00:17:37.183 --> 00:17:40.763
In the preserved Orion call, the model selected Orion

00:17:40.763 --> 00:17:41.743
Clinical Platform,

00:17:42.723 --> 00:17:43.363
Web APIs,

00:17:44.183 --> 00:17:45.863
FastAPI, and Python.

00:17:46.652 --> 00:17:49.152
All four assignments cited evidence one.

00:17:50.541 --> 00:17:52.101
Forge and Package Management were omitted.

00:17:53.569 --> 00:17:57.069
The request counted seven hundred sixty input tokens and

00:17:57.069 --> 00:17:59.349
returned one hundred ninety-five output tokens.

00:18:00.578 --> 00:18:04.278
This visible result does not expose the model's private

00:18:04.278 --> 00:18:05.378
reasoning process.

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:13.030
Validation checks active IDs,

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:14.010
kinds,

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:15.370
workspace ownership,

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:16.750
allowed candidates,

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:18.990
duplicates, field limits,

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:21.270
status, and evidence references.

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:24.770
Dispatch and commit also check access,

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:26.130
profile hashes,

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:28.510
revisions, and user decisions.

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:32.230
Suggestions remain proposals until accepted.

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:36.910
A real evidence ID may still cite irrelevant prose,

00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:39.770
and the model's confidence is not a calibrated accuracy

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:40.490
probability.

00:18:45.714 --> 00:18:48.934
Luna is the task default supported by the limited

00:18:48.934 --> 00:18:50.234
classification tests;

00:18:50.914 --> 00:18:52.874
Sol supplied the taxonomy draft.

00:18:54.284 --> 00:18:57.464
A comprehensive model-winner study was not completed.

00:18:59.354 --> 00:19:03.174
The audit also found evidence-ID validation broader than the

00:19:03.174 --> 00:19:06.874
transmitted compact set, and a taxonomy prompt limit of

00:19:06.874 --> 00:19:09.694
twenty versus a validator limit of fifty.

00:19:11.244 --> 00:19:14.204
Those are improvement tasks, not shipped guarantees.

00:19:19.427 --> 00:19:20.027
Section ten.

00:19:21.577 --> 00:19:23.637
Counterexamples and failure cases.

00:19:25.407 --> 00:19:27.927
Their purpose is to show where an apparently sensible

00:19:27.927 --> 00:19:29.547
pipeline can mislead us.

00:19:30.777 --> 00:19:34.537
We keep the confusing evidence visible rather than explaining

00:19:34.537 --> 00:19:36.397
only the clean success case.

00:19:45.753 --> 00:19:48.913
One fixture explicitly says it is not part of

00:19:48.913 --> 00:19:49.873
Helios or Orion.

00:19:51.743 --> 00:19:55.243
Lexical names still retrieve both Projects, but the saved

00:19:55.243 --> 00:19:59.923
classifier selects HTTP Clients and Python with neither Project.

00:20:01.473 --> 00:20:04.593
Another audit fixture genuinely supports two initiatives.

00:20:05.823 --> 00:20:07.723
The task must allow both.

00:20:09.193 --> 00:20:11.873
A forced single winner would change the meaning of

00:20:11.873 --> 00:20:12.533
organization.

00:20:17.887 --> 00:20:22.167
The full FastAPI profile contains its purpose statement, but

00:20:22.167 --> 00:20:26.667
an uppercase title marker let documentation links occupy compact

00:20:26.667 --> 00:20:27.047
slots.

00:20:28.562 --> 00:20:31.442
Retrieval could see evidence the generator did not receive.

00:20:32.698 --> 00:20:36.418
Metadata still supported the saved answer, Web APIs and

00:20:36.418 --> 00:20:36.818
Python.

00:20:37.493 --> 00:20:40.773
An earlier answer added unwanted secondary labels.

00:20:42.069 --> 00:20:46.348
Primary-only policy clarified the task, but reused cases cannot

00:20:46.348 --> 00:20:49.009
establish an independent causal improvement.

00:20:54.807 --> 00:20:59.047
Empty, fork-only, and metadata-only cases need no-match or

00:20:59.047 --> 00:21:00.047
uncertainty paths.

00:21:01.164 --> 00:21:03.844
Installation noise can introduce unrelated names.

00:21:05.081 --> 00:21:07.021
English extraction can miss other languages.

00:21:07.297 --> 00:21:11.877
Narrow cleaning can miss malicious instructions or secret-like

00:21:11.877 --> 00:21:12.197
text.

00:21:13.274 --> 00:21:16.694
These fixtures explore boundaries; they are not a comprehensive

00:21:16.694 --> 00:21:17.834
security benchmark.

00:21:18.971 --> 00:21:22.171
Next, we preserve the decisions and uncertainty that follow

00:21:22.171 --> 00:21:23.071
from these cases.

00:21:28.683 --> 00:21:29.183
Section eleven.

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:31.610
Memory and user authority.

00:21:32.856 --> 00:21:35.756
The purpose is to preserve useful state across changes.

00:21:37.302 --> 00:21:39.262
Here, memory means application records,

00:21:39.922 --> 00:21:42.922
not a model remembering a conversation or a LangChain

00:21:42.922 --> 00:21:44.502
conversation-memory component.

00:21:54.107 --> 00:21:54.547
Relationships,

00:21:55.347 --> 00:21:55.987
completed analysis,

00:21:56.707 --> 00:21:59.927
freshness, and review status answer different questions.

00:22:00.671 --> 00:22:04.091
A successful no-match is completed analysis.

00:22:05.114 --> 00:22:08.574
Removing Orion's Project can leave its Topic and Tags

00:22:08.574 --> 00:22:10.554
useful, while the receipt remains.

00:22:12.118 --> 00:22:15.578
Provider replay cache and optional run history are different

00:22:15.578 --> 00:22:16.038
records.

00:22:17.542 --> 00:22:20.542
Deleting one display or membership does not silently make

00:22:20.542 --> 00:22:23.602
the repository eligible for another paid decision.

00:22:29.143 --> 00:22:31.723
Accepting a proposal creates a user decision.

00:22:33.439 --> 00:22:36.779
Rejecting or removing a relationship leaves a protected tombstone.

00:22:38.115 --> 00:22:41.895
Approved rules can supply deterministic mappings, subject to those

00:22:41.895 --> 00:22:42.455
rejections.

00:22:43.951 --> 00:22:47.851
Ordinary organization cannot recreate a rejected edge behind the

00:22:47.851 --> 00:22:48.511
user's back.

00:22:49.247 --> 00:22:51.467
These protections preserve authority;

00:22:52.087 --> 00:22:55.507
they do not prove every accepted relationship was independently

00:22:55.507 --> 00:22:56.527
verified truth.

00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:05.490
Local reconciliation applies approved rules, compatible stored

00:23:05.490 --> 00:23:09.910
assignments, or contiguous name and alias matches for review.

00:23:11.359 --> 00:23:14.979
This match is stricter than retrieval's unordered alias tokens.

00:23:16.728 --> 00:23:20.468
Local suggestions have visible provenance and zero model

00:23:20.468 --> 00:23:20.968
confidence.

00:23:22.537 --> 00:23:24.617
They do not manufacture AI completion.

00:23:26.426 --> 00:23:29.986
Fresh analysis remains available with an explicit reason and

00:23:29.986 --> 00:23:32.666
reviewed budget when the user wants a new judgment.

00:23:38.137 --> 00:23:38.937
Section twelve.

00:23:40.707 --> 00:23:41.247
Loop engineering.

00:23:42.757 --> 00:23:45.557
Its purpose is to control transitions around inference.

00:23:46.807 --> 00:23:49.507
We need to know when to run, when to

00:23:49.507 --> 00:23:52.187
skip, and when a result has become unsafe to

00:23:52.187 --> 00:23:52.487
apply.

00:23:54.457 --> 00:23:55.917
This is application control,

00:23:56.677 --> 00:23:59.117
not an autonomous model thought-and-action loop.

00:24:08.580 --> 00:24:11.640
Preview and worker check admission before constructing the

00:24:11.640 --> 00:24:13.700
provider or making a count request.

00:24:15.189 --> 00:24:19.108
Transactions claim running attempts so concurrent starts do not

00:24:19.108 --> 00:24:21.209
independently process the same operation.

00:24:22.797 --> 00:24:25.937
Previously attempted or uncertain work requires deliberate review,

00:24:26.517 --> 00:24:27.557
not a silent retry.

00:24:29.106 --> 00:24:32.806
Explicit re-analysis can bypass memoization while retaining

00:24:32.806 --> 00:24:33.446
privacy,

00:24:34.246 --> 00:24:35.626
schema, and spending checks.

00:24:36.994 --> 00:24:40.814
Classification cohorts use new-analysis, Project, and recency

00:24:40.814 --> 00:24:42.734
ordering, not a learned ranker.

00:24:47.808 --> 00:24:51.888
Automatic organization accumulates eligible changes.

00:24:53.388 --> 00:24:56.928
Defaults combine weight six and three distinct entities,

00:24:57.588 --> 00:24:58.928
or two new Projects,

00:24:59.988 --> 00:25:03.248
followed by a ninety-second quiet period and a thirty-minute

00:25:03.248 --> 00:25:04.968
cooldown.

00:25:04.968 --> 00:25:06.848
Types and thresholds are configurable.

00:25:08.148 --> 00:25:10.968
Consumed event sequences prevent endless rescheduling.

00:25:12.188 --> 00:25:14.508
Existing analysis still reconciles locally.

00:25:15.288 --> 00:25:18.668
A change upstream cannot be noticed before its content

00:25:18.668 --> 00:25:19.348
is fetched.

00:25:25.140 --> 00:25:29.380
Revision, generation, policy, and epoch fences bind a response

00:25:29.380 --> 00:25:30.300
to current state.

00:25:31.500 --> 00:25:34.540
If the user edits or resets during generation,

00:25:35.440 --> 00:25:39.720
unsafe associations are discarded while historical cost and

00:25:39.720 --> 00:25:40.560
processing evidence remain.

00:25:41.760 --> 00:25:43.040
Reset uses a scoped,

00:25:44.100 --> 00:25:47.260
expiring, one-use preview and exact confirmation.

00:25:48.060 --> 00:25:51.420
It preserves cost history and readiness reports.

00:25:52.500 --> 00:25:56.340
These are tested local safeguards, not distributed exactly-once

00:25:56.340 --> 00:25:58.540
execution or forensic erasure.

00:26:04.287 --> 00:26:05.147
Section thirteen.

00:26:06.657 --> 00:26:07.477
Harness engineering.

00:26:09.067 --> 00:26:11.507
Its purpose is to make a model request measurable

00:26:11.507 --> 00:26:13.807
and bounded before it leaves the application.

00:26:15.637 --> 00:26:19.237
A successful connection alone tells us nothing about decision

00:26:19.237 --> 00:26:19.697
quality,

00:26:20.397 --> 00:26:22.497
safe state changes, or total cost.

00:26:31.443 --> 00:26:35.923
The provider inspects the serialized LangChain request, including

00:26:35.923 --> 00:26:36.603
destination,

00:26:37.283 --> 00:26:37.603
model,

00:26:38.663 --> 00:26:38.783
instructions,

00:26:39.443 --> 00:26:39.563
schema,

00:26:40.243 --> 00:26:43.263
output limits, and disabled tool or conversation fields.

00:26:44.423 --> 00:26:48.703
The HTTP hook checks current session and workspace authorization.

00:26:50.083 --> 00:26:52.123
Counting consumes an HTTP attempt.

00:26:53.243 --> 00:26:56.883
Only a successful bounded count permits a monetary reservation

00:26:56.883 --> 00:26:57.843
and generation.

00:26:57.843 --> 00:27:02.423
SDK retries are disabled to prevent hidden request

00:27:02.423 --> 00:27:03.503
multiplication.

00:27:09.063 --> 00:27:11.443
Known valid usage settles the estimate.

00:27:12.846 --> 00:27:16.286
Refusal or incomplete output is not a successful replay

00:27:16.286 --> 00:27:18.386
entry, but can still cost tokens.

00:27:19.948 --> 00:27:20.568
Missing usage,

00:27:21.188 --> 00:27:24.568
timeout, and uncertain failures keep the maximum reservation.

00:27:26.011 --> 00:27:28.491
A bound violation stops later paid admission.

00:27:29.873 --> 00:27:33.313
Selected provider rejections have a specific local accounting

00:27:33.313 --> 00:27:33.893
policy;

00:27:34.933 --> 00:27:37.773
none of these estimates is independent invoice reconciliation.

00:27:43.793 --> 00:27:46.853
Fixed mode has audited request and generation limits.

00:27:48.184 --> 00:27:51.684
Selective renewal or override preserves past attempts and

00:27:51.684 --> 00:27:51.804
spending.

00:27:53.114 --> 00:27:56.294
Adaptive mode admits a finite reviewed dollar grant under

00:27:56.294 --> 00:27:57.754
the same cumulative cap.

00:27:58.944 --> 00:28:02.484
Per-call reservations transfer from a run hold without double

00:28:02.484 --> 00:28:02.895
counting.

00:28:02.895 --> 00:28:05.795
Recovery links holds to jobs,

00:28:06.695 --> 00:28:10.175
releases unused terminal money, and preserves unknown-call holds.

00:28:11.665 --> 00:28:14.625
Separate local databases still require reconciliation.

00:28:20.323 --> 00:28:21.443
Section fourteen.

00:28:22.752 --> 00:28:24.032
Tokenomics and optimization.

00:28:25.461 --> 00:28:28.181
The purpose is to understand what each decision consumes

00:28:28.181 --> 00:28:30.061
and which costs can be avoided.

00:28:31.570 --> 00:28:33.330
We separate historical estimates,

00:28:34.170 --> 00:28:37.050
conservative admission bounds, and the broader cost of a

00:28:37.050 --> 00:28:38.710
useful accepted relationship.

00:28:48.560 --> 00:28:51.620
The harness pins a rate snapshot and counts assembled

00:28:51.620 --> 00:28:52.020
input.

00:28:53.730 --> 00:28:57.190
It reserves possible output, a conservative cache-write allowance,

00:28:57.690 --> 00:29:00.030
and headroom without assuming a cache discount.

00:29:01.980 --> 00:29:04.880
Known usage later settles in integer microdollars.

00:29:06.730 --> 00:29:09.670
Reasoning tokens already belong to output and must not

00:29:09.670 --> 00:29:10.570
be added twice.

00:29:11.780 --> 00:29:15.460
A maximum-output reservation is not a prediction of the

00:29:15.460 --> 00:29:16.680
answer's usual length.

00:29:22.327 --> 00:29:26.447
The twenty-case API round made twenty generation requests and

00:29:26.447 --> 00:29:27.927
twenty input-count requests:

00:29:28.727 --> 00:29:31.067
forty provider HTTP operations.

00:29:32.267 --> 00:29:36.367
It recorded sixteen thousand forty-one input tokens and three

00:29:36.367 --> 00:29:38.927
thousand four hundred fourteen output tokens.

00:29:39.967 --> 00:29:43.567
The rounded inference estimate was about three-tenths of a

00:29:43.567 --> 00:29:43.687
cent.

00:29:44.447 --> 00:29:45.967
This excludes media,

00:29:46.927 --> 00:29:48.987
infrastructure, indexing, and human review;

00:29:50.247 --> 00:29:52.187
it is not a production cost guarantee.

00:29:58.363 --> 00:29:59.043
Compact evidence,

00:29:59.903 --> 00:30:03.883
candidate caps, and bounded collection sampling reduce individual

00:30:03.883 --> 00:30:06.683
requests, but can omit useful context.

00:30:08.223 --> 00:30:10.943
Receipts and local reconciliation can avoid another request

00:30:10.943 --> 00:30:11.523
entirely.

00:30:12.923 --> 00:30:16.123
Provider prompt caching still invokes a model, and no

00:30:16.123 --> 00:30:18.123
discount benefit appeared in that round.

00:30:19.523 --> 00:30:19.943
Count latency,

00:30:20.863 --> 00:30:21.383
evidence refresh,

00:30:22.303 --> 00:30:24.703
storage, and reviewer corrections also matter.

00:30:25.903 --> 00:30:29.543
Optimize cost per correct, accepted, current association.

00:30:35.077 --> 00:30:36.037
Section fifteen.

00:30:37.257 --> 00:30:37.997
Evaluation and evidence.

00:30:38.677 --> 00:30:41.137
The purpose is to learn which stage succeeds,

00:30:41.937 --> 00:30:45.317
which stage fails, and how far the measurements generalize.

00:30:45.867 --> 00:30:50.682
A single attractive score cannot answer all three

00:30:50.682 --> 00:30:51.122
questions.

00:31:00.613 --> 00:31:03.233
The frozen corpus has thirty repositories.

00:31:04.373 --> 00:31:05.733
Ten were development cases;

00:31:06.773 --> 00:31:10.653
twenty formed the evaluation partition, with eight public

00:31:10.653 --> 00:31:13.233
libraries and twelve synthetic cases.

00:31:13.973 --> 00:31:16.433
The registry has forty-two concepts,

00:31:17.093 --> 00:31:19.433
including four non-searchable Domains.

00:31:20.273 --> 00:31:23.593
Public labels were proposed and user-approved.

00:31:24.693 --> 00:31:28.673
Related initiatives were grouped, but policy clarification reused

00:31:28.673 --> 00:31:29.853
evaluation cases.

00:31:30.893 --> 00:31:32.813
The final round is regression validation,

00:31:33.613 --> 00:31:35.873
not untouched generalization evidence.

00:31:37.073 --> 00:31:39.313
Project-positive evidence is synthetic;

00:31:40.553 --> 00:31:43.133
private enterprise performance remains unestablished.

00:31:48.813 --> 00:31:52.793
Candidate recall asks whether expected IDs reached the shortlist.

00:31:53.674 --> 00:31:58.414
Both lexical methods covered all expected evaluation labels under

00:31:58.414 --> 00:31:59.354
generous caps.

00:32:00.915 --> 00:32:03.355
Classification then produced fifty true positives,

00:32:04.135 --> 00:32:06.515
zero false positives, and two misses:

00:32:07.555 --> 00:32:10.735
micro F one of ninety-eight percent.

00:32:10.735 --> 00:32:13.115
Both missing labels had been retrieved,

00:32:14.155 --> 00:32:17.515
locating those errors after candidate inclusion, without proving

00:32:17.515 --> 00:32:19.935
whether packing or model selection caused them.

00:32:25.413 --> 00:32:29.433
Taxonomy drafts passed structural checks and received qualitative

00:32:29.433 --> 00:32:33.133
acceptance, but no numeric human rubric was recorded.

00:32:34.313 --> 00:32:36.073
One repeated classification agreed;

00:32:36.753 --> 00:32:38.553
that is not long-run stability.

00:32:39.953 --> 00:32:40.373
Limited timing,

00:32:41.093 --> 00:32:42.213
contract, race,

00:32:43.133 --> 00:32:46.673
privacy, and recovery checks establish specific behaviors.

00:32:47.553 --> 00:32:51.393
They do not measure citation entailment or calibrated confidence.

00:32:52.173 --> 00:32:56.253
No complete RAGAS-style question-answering evaluation or

00:32:56.253 --> 00:32:58.993
independent production accuracy study was performed.

00:33:00.553 --> 00:33:03.333
Historical timings use nearest-rank percentiles from twenty

00:33:03.333 --> 00:33:03.873
observations,

00:33:04.873 --> 00:33:06.033
not a production guarantee.

00:33:07.433 --> 00:33:10.393
Subscription-based Codex checks were supplementary, not

00:33:10.393 --> 00:33:12.793
replacements for real API validation.

00:33:17.953 --> 00:33:21.113
A stronger study needs independent annotations,

00:33:21.973 --> 00:33:26.213
unseen initiatives, harder neighbors, no-match cases, and broader

00:33:26.213 --> 00:33:26.753
languages.

00:33:28.053 --> 00:33:30.933
Freeze policy and source snapshots before comparing methods.

00:33:32.173 --> 00:33:35.733
Group related repositories when splitting, and report per-kind

00:33:35.733 --> 00:33:36.213
errors,

00:33:37.033 --> 00:33:37.153
abstention,

00:33:37.893 --> 00:33:38.373
source support,

00:33:39.173 --> 00:33:41.193
correction effort, and total cost.

00:33:42.153 --> 00:33:44.913
Confidence intervals and model-winner claims should follow

00:33:44.913 --> 00:33:49.153
adequate data rather than being manufactured from this small

00:33:49.153 --> 00:33:50.013
reused set.

00:33:55.143 --> 00:33:56.323
Section sixteen.

00:33:57.023 --> 00:34:00.263
Stronger retrieval and contextual retrieval.

00:34:00.463 --> 00:34:04.023
The purpose is to investigate specific weaknesses without

00:34:04.023 --> 00:34:07.043
mistaking architectural complexity for improvement.

00:34:08.143 --> 00:34:11.243
Everything in the research lane is a proposal or

00:34:11.243 --> 00:34:12.083
external reference,

00:34:12.903 --> 00:34:14.523
not a current product capability.

00:34:24.023 --> 00:34:24.603
First

00:34:25.363 --> 00:34:26.423
preserve complete sentences,

00:34:27.443 --> 00:34:29.283
decisive passages, and contradiction.

00:34:30.611 --> 00:34:34.091
Align evidence validation with exactly what was transmitted.

00:34:35.799 --> 00:34:38.859
Compare candidate-conditioned passage selection with today's

00:34:38.859 --> 00:34:41.379
simple packing at the same token ceiling.

00:34:42.967 --> 00:34:44.967
Sparse experiments can vary term frequency,

00:34:45.627 --> 00:34:46.207
field weights,

00:34:47.027 --> 00:34:47.427
alias order,

00:34:48.107 --> 00:34:49.487
boosts, and smaller caps.

00:34:50.695 --> 00:34:53.915
These tests ask which error is fixed, rather than

00:34:53.915 --> 00:34:55.615
assuming the next layer must be better.

00:35:00.333 --> 00:35:05.173
A public-only bi-encoder trial could embed concept definitions and

00:35:05.173 --> 00:35:07.473
repository-purpose profiles separately.

00:35:08.192 --> 00:35:12.412
A small registry can use exact local similarity before

00:35:12.412 --> 00:35:14.052
an approximate-neighbor service.

00:35:15.450 --> 00:35:17.670
Cache by content and encoder version;

00:35:18.510 --> 00:35:20.610
preserve identity and access metadata.

00:35:21.529 --> 00:35:24.249
If dense search recovers real lexical misses,

00:35:25.169 --> 00:35:28.389
compare sparse and dense unions with reciprocal-rank fusion.

00:35:29.388 --> 00:35:33.028
A reranker adds cost and cannot recover a candidate

00:35:33.028 --> 00:35:34.347
absent from that union.

00:35:35.846 --> 00:35:38.646
Private embeddings are derived content and need separate

00:35:38.646 --> 00:35:39.126
permission.

00:35:44.413 --> 00:35:46.733
Now, contextual retrieval.

00:35:47.593 --> 00:35:50.013
Its purpose is to make an indexed chunk meaningful

00:35:50.013 --> 00:35:51.673
beyond its isolated words.

00:35:52.653 --> 00:35:56.433
Anthropic's approach adds document-conditioned context before

00:35:56.433 --> 00:36:02.233
indexing chunks with embeddings and BM25, with optional reranking.

00:36:02.233 --> 00:36:05.873
Our deterministic metadata and purpose excerpts are not that

00:36:05.873 --> 00:36:06.433
mechanism.

00:36:07.493 --> 00:36:11.133
A trial could compare cheap metadata prefixes with generated

00:36:11.133 --> 00:36:11.793
context,

00:36:12.793 --> 00:36:13.713
accounting for indexing,

00:36:14.493 --> 00:36:14.613
refresh,

00:36:15.413 --> 00:36:17.133
privacy, and downstream support.

00:36:18.213 --> 00:36:21.813
External published results do not become measured GitHub Manager

00:36:21.813 --> 00:36:24.873
improvements merely by showing the reference diagram.

00:36:29.942 --> 00:36:34.204
A future controller could allow one extra source-linked evidence

00:36:34.204 --> 00:36:37.144
pass after an insufficient-context result,

00:36:37.844 --> 00:36:41.044
under a reviewed budget, then abstain.

00:36:42.484 --> 00:36:45.824
Adaptive RAG, Self-RAG, and corrective RAG are research

00:36:45.824 --> 00:36:46.304
references,

00:36:47.064 --> 00:36:48.564
not adopted implementations.

00:36:49.524 --> 00:36:52.904
Agentic retrieval would additionally need tool permissions and

00:36:52.904 --> 00:36:54.044
trajectory evaluation.

00:36:55.104 --> 00:36:59.284
Domain relationships alone do not create GraphRAG.

00:36:59.284 --> 00:37:02.604
Application memory does not make the model remember conversations.

00:37:08.070 --> 00:37:08.890
Section seventeen.

00:37:10.740 --> 00:37:12.960
Decision models, and the Jev research question.

00:37:14.700 --> 00:37:17.790
The purpose is to investigate whether a specialized decision

00:37:17.790 --> 00:37:21.810
interface could improve bounded judgments after the options are

00:37:21.810 --> 00:37:21.930
known.

00:37:23.640 --> 00:37:26.600
No Jev integration or live Jev test has been

00:37:26.600 --> 00:37:27.320
performed here.

00:37:35.833 --> 00:37:38.353
TypeSafe describes Choice,

00:37:39.093 --> 00:37:41.173
Score, and Noul primitives for typed judgments.

00:37:41.567 --> 00:37:45.347
For repository organization, a candidate could be supported,

00:37:46.147 --> 00:37:47.587
unsupported, or unclear.

00:37:48.941 --> 00:37:52.141
Ask separately for each candidate when several memberships are

00:37:52.141 --> 00:37:52.581
possible.

00:37:53.914 --> 00:37:57.974
Open-ended taxonomy discovery still needs generation to propose

00:37:57.974 --> 00:37:59.254
new names and definitions.

00:38:00.548 --> 00:38:03.728
A choice among existing options cannot replace that creative

00:38:03.728 --> 00:38:04.748
vocabulary step.

00:38:10.340 --> 00:38:14.000
A probability-derived decision confidence is not the same as

00:38:14.000 --> 00:38:17.920
today's generated confidence number, and neither proves task

00:38:17.920 --> 00:38:18.540
calibration.

00:38:20.178 --> 00:38:21.998
A shadow study should retain the baseline,

00:38:22.738 --> 00:38:24.018
test negation and option order,

00:38:24.658 --> 00:38:26.178
and measure high-confidence errors,

00:38:26.838 --> 00:38:27.118
abstention,

00:38:27.818 --> 00:38:30.298
fallback, review effort, and total spending.

00:38:31.975 --> 00:38:36.275
Extra provider credentials, retention terms, retries, and failures

00:38:36.275 --> 00:38:37.755
require their own controls.

00:38:39.573 --> 00:38:42.413
Faster decisions do not guarantee better completed workflows.

00:38:48.260 --> 00:38:51.400
Potential uses include candidate filtering, passage relevance,

00:38:52.180 --> 00:38:54.500
duplicate-review triage, or bounded assignment.

00:38:55.620 --> 00:38:57.720
Any filter can discard a correct candidate.

00:38:58.860 --> 00:38:59.320
Budget arithmetic,

00:39:00.240 --> 00:39:02.200
privacy policy, stable-ID validity,

00:39:02.980 --> 00:39:06.180
rejections, and stale-state protection stay deterministic.

00:39:07.540 --> 00:39:10.620
Adoption should require a measured quality-cost tradeoff on

00:39:10.620 --> 00:39:11.400
independent data,

00:39:12.020 --> 00:39:12.920
not a vendor headline.

00:39:13.740 --> 00:39:17.160
We finish by following the entire current workflow once

00:39:17.160 --> 00:39:17.440
more.

00:39:23.060 --> 00:39:24.320
Section eighteen.

00:39:25.750 --> 00:39:27.310
The complete trace and next steps.

00:39:29.260 --> 00:39:31.580
The purpose is to reconnect the technical layers to

00:39:31.580 --> 00:39:32.440
the original need:

00:39:33.320 --> 00:39:34.480
find useful repositories,

00:39:35.660 --> 00:39:38.920
understand why they belong together, and keep control as

00:39:38.920 --> 00:39:39.980
the collection changes.

00:39:49.690 --> 00:39:52.890
Orion's source sentence explains patient intake, the clinical

00:39:52.890 --> 00:39:53.370
initiative,

00:39:54.130 --> 00:39:55.670
FastAPI, and Python.

00:39:56.750 --> 00:39:58.870
Local extraction retains evidence one.

00:39:59.710 --> 00:40:01.150
Retrieval finds six possibilities.

00:40:01.950 --> 00:40:03.770
Augmentation supplies evidence,

00:40:04.690 --> 00:40:04.810
definitions,

00:40:05.550 --> 00:40:07.230
policy, and schema.

00:40:07.470 --> 00:40:09.650
Generation returns four supported IDs.

00:40:11.130 --> 00:40:13.710
Validation and review establish usable relationships.

00:40:14.610 --> 00:40:17.550
A receipt preserves completed work even if the user

00:40:17.550 --> 00:40:18.870
later removes a Project.

00:40:24.610 --> 00:40:29.310
Readiness phases, frozen corpora, source hashes, lockfiles,

00:40:29.310 --> 00:40:32.590
reports, and historical ledgers preserve what was actually tested.

00:40:33.710 --> 00:40:37.430
Reconstructing a request offline is not recovering an original

00:40:37.430 --> 00:40:38.010
wire log.

00:40:38.590 --> 00:40:42.510
This animation does not rerun application or model benchmarks.

00:40:43.430 --> 00:40:44.850
The original academic,

00:40:45.470 --> 00:40:48.730
illustrated, and publication editions remain available with exact

00:40:48.730 --> 00:40:49.130
inputs,

00:40:50.090 --> 00:40:50.210
formulas,

00:40:50.830 --> 00:40:52.350
qualifications, and references.

00:40:58.383 --> 00:41:00.583
The next steps are better evidence packing,

00:41:01.303 --> 00:41:02.343
tighter validation parity,

00:41:03.083 --> 00:41:07.003
independent evaluation, and only then conditional retrieval or

00:41:07.003 --> 00:41:08.363
decision-model experiments.

00:41:09.310 --> 00:41:13.010
Cloud migration needs separate concurrency and recovery

00:41:13.010 --> 00:41:13.630
validation.

00:41:15.077 --> 00:41:16.837
The practical habit is simple:

00:41:17.497 --> 00:41:21.817
put the source, shortlist, request, answer, and resulting state

00:41:21.817 --> 00:41:22.757
beside one another.

00:41:24.464 --> 00:41:25.424
Change one user decision,

00:41:26.124 --> 00:41:28.504
follow the next run, and measure what improved.
